  "title": "Job 12",
  "display_title": "Job 12",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "job",
  "book": "Job",
  "bookName": "Job",
  "bookOrder": 18,
  "testament": "old",
  "chapter": 12,
  "sortOrder": 18012,
  "verseCount": 25,
  "aliases": [
    "Job"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:12:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "And Job answered and said,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 12:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:12:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:12:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "No doubt but ye are the people, and wisdom shall die with you.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 12:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:12:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:12:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "But I have understanding as well as you; I am not inferior to you: yea, who knoweth not such things as these?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 12:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:12:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:12:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "I am as one mocked of his neighbour, who calleth upon God, and he answereth him: the just upright man is laughed to scorn.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 12:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:12:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:12:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "He that is ready to slip with his feet is as a lamp despised in the thought of him that is at ease.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 12:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:12:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:12:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "The tabernacles of robbers prosper, and they that provoke God are secure; into whose hand God bringeth abundantly.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 12:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:12:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:12:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "But ask now the beasts, and they shall teach thee; and the fowls of the air, and they shall tell thee:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 12:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:12:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:12:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "Or speak to the earth, and it shall teach thee: and the fishes of the sea shall declare unto thee.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 12:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:12:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:12:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "Who knoweth not in all these that the hand of the LORD hath wrought this?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 12:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:12:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:12:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "In whose hand is the soul of every living thing, and the breath of all mankind.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 12:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:12:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:12:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "Doth not the ear try words? and the mouth taste his meat?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 12:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:12:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:12:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "With the ancient is wisdom; and in length of days understanding.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 12:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:12:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:12:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "With him is wisdom and strength, he hath counsel and understanding.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 12:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:12:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:12:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "Behold, he breaketh down, and it cannot be built again: he shutteth up a man, and there can be no opening.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 12:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:12:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:12:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "Behold, he withholdeth the waters, and they dry up: also he sendeth them out, and they overturn the earth.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 12:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:12:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:12:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "With him is strength and wisdom: the deceived and the deceiver are his.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 12:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:12:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:12:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "He leadeth counsellors away spoiled, and maketh the judges fools.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 12:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:12:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:12:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "He looseth the bond of kings, and girdeth their loins with a girdle.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 12:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:12:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:12:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "He leadeth princes away spoiled, and overthroweth the mighty.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 12:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:12:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:12:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "He removeth away the speech of the trusty, and taketh away the understanding of the aged.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 12:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:12:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:12:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "He poureth contempt upon princes, and weakeneth the strength of the mighty.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 12:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:12:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:12:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "He discovereth deep things out of darkness, and bringeth out to light the shadow of death.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 12:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:12:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:12:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "He increaseth the nations, and destroyeth them: he enlargeth the nations, and straiteneth them again.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 12:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:12:23"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-024",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 24,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:12:24",
      "numberLabel": "24",
      "text": "He taketh away the heart of the chief of the people of the earth, and causeth them to wander in a wilderness where there is no way.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 12:24",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:12:24"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-025",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 25,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:12:25",
      "numberLabel": "25",
      "text": "They grope in the dark without light, and he maketh them to stagger like a drunken man.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 12:25",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:12:25"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
